  "id": "effort-justification",
  "term": "effort justification",
  "definition": "Effort justification is a cognitive dissonance idea that putting in more effort can lead a person to value the outcome or reward more. In this paradigm, the subjective feeling of greater effort is linked to increased reward valuation, including on implicit measures.",
